,"position":"1787395014311350001-68101444-020f-45da-88df-bc78177c1f09"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6814a0b00a80723778a2d65886daf33c55d6a7dd1a097296b0b731ae386eebaf","event_uuid":"671c3171-d36d-44e7-aadf-6fb676bc4613","position":{"commit_sha":"c761988a14ab421b3d53cd6bdcb7e47d2dbf59a4","position":"1787395019991575001-671c3171-d36d-44e7-aadf-6fb676bc4613"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision (2026-08-19): APPROVED — model the predicate with an operator-tagged union / dataclass per operator family, exactly as the description's Approach proposes. Do NOT widen to `value: Any`, and do NOT reach for cast().\n\nRationale: `value: object` produces 7 real mypy errors in the body and `Any` would satisfy the ratchet while buying neither navigability nor a contract driver — the documented failure mode on cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8. The tagged union is the only option that actually buys the contract, because the operator and its value shape travel together and the body narrows by construction. An @overload-on-operator-literal alternative was considered: it introduces less new vocabulary but still leaves the body needing narrowing, so it solves less for comparable effort.\n\nBlast radius is contained: there are only two callers to update (reducer/_query.py and apply_ticket_filters), which is what makes this affordable.","timestamp":1787173867217736001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented: PredicateValue op-tagged union (str | AbstractSet[str] | (lo,hi) tuple) in reducer/_filters.py; match_predicate annotated and narrowed by construction via per-field helpers extracted along the existing tag/priority/string-field seams (C901 17 -> 3, stale baseline entry left for maintenance). _parse_value now returns tuple[str, PredicateValue]; search_states pass-through verified by the package-wide mypy run, no signature change. rebar.reducer.* promoted into tier-1 override + _RATCHET_BASELINE. mypy src/rebar/reducer clean, no new Any; existing query/search/filter tests pass unmodified; lint/typecheck/complexity gates green. Gerrit change 2065.","timestamp":1787375030965046001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged: Gerrit change 2065 → commit aed259e33b (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). match_predicate now takes PredicateValue (str | AbstractSet[str] | tuple[str|None,str|None]); rebar.reducer.* joined the tier-1 mypy ratchet. Patchset 1's Verified -1 was the manifest -dirty flake, root-caused and fixed as discovered bug b44c-2a74 (change 2088, merged); patchset 2 (rebase) went green.","timestamp":1787394355284662001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1786649288703967001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5f2539db-aa4f-487d-a8bf-295183818f29","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1"},{"link_uuid":"a0e5dc26-f1dd-486a-a5b0-29a86ac3b753","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eb49-3f52-e95e-4332"}],"description":"## Context\nSplit out of 06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1 (effete-barbaric-xiaosaurus). `reducer` is ONE\nun-annotated def away from the tier-1 typing ratchet — but that one def is not a\nrubber-stamp annotation, which is why it was excluded rather than papered over.\n\n## The problem\n`rebar.reducer._filters.match_predicate(state, field, op, value)` takes `value` whose\ntype DEPENDS ON `op`: a scalar for `eq`/`lt`/`le`/`gt`/`ge`, an iterable for `in`, and a\n`(lo, hi)` pair for `range`. Annotating it `value: object` was tried and produces 7 real\nmypy errors in the body (`object` is not iterable, no `int()` overload, etc.).\n`value: Any` would satisfy the ratchet while buying neither the navigability nor the\ncontract driver — exactly the failure mode ticket cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8 documents.\n\n## Approach\nModel the predicate properly rather than widening: an operator-tagged `PredicateValue`\nunion defined in `_filters.py` (a `str` scalar for `eq`/`lt`/`le`/`gt`/`ge`, an\n`AbstractSet[str]` for `in`, and a `tuple[str | None, str | None]` pair for `range`), so\nthe operator and its value shape travel together and the body narrows by construction\n(isinstance narrowing inside per-field helpers extracted along the existing\ntag/priority/string-field seams — which also brings `match_predicate`'s baselined\nC901=17 DOWN, never up). The value has three in-package consumers/producers, all\ncovered:\n\n1. `reducer/_query.py` — `_parse_value` PRODUCES the value; tighten its return to\n   `tuple[str, PredicateValue]` so the parser builds exactly the shape the matcher\n   consumes.\n2. `reducer/_filters.py::apply_ticket_filters` — builds `set[str]` values for `in` and a\n   scalar for `eq`; already conforms, now checked against the annotation.\n3. `reducer/search.py::search_states` (line ~206) — the pass-through: unpacks\n   `(f, op, val, neg)` tuples from `parse_query` (and its `parent_resolver` rewrite maps\n   an `eq` str value to another str, shape-preserving) and forwards `val` to\n   `match_predicate`. The forwarded value stays inside the `PredicateValue` union by\n   construction; the module is re-verified under\n   `mypy src/rebar/reducer --disallow-untyped-defs` like the rest of the package, and no\n   signature change is expected there (the existing `match_predicate(state, field, op,\n   value)` call shape is preserved, so `search.py` and the unit tests keep passing\n   unmodified).\n\nThen promote `rebar.reducer.*` into the tier-1 override in pyproject.toml and\n`_RATCHET_BASELINE` in tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `mypy src/rebar/reducer --disallow-untyped-defs` is clean with NO new `: Any`/`-> Any`.\n- [x] `rebar.reducer.*` is in the tier-1 override and pinned in `_RATCHET_BASELINE`.\n- [x] Filter/query behaviour is unchanged (existing reducer filter tests pass unmodified).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_filters.py","reason":"Define the op-tagged PredicateValue union (str scalar | AbstractSet[str] for in | (lo,hi) pair for range), annotate match_predicate with it, and narrow by construction via per-field helpers extracted along the existing tag/priority/string-field seams (also brings the baselined C901=17 down instead of up)."},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_query.py","reason":"Tighten _parse_value to return tuple[str, PredicateValue] so the parser builds the same tagged value shape the matcher consumes."},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/search.py","reason":"Third consumer: search_states forwards parse_query predicate values to match_predicate; re-verified under mypy --disallow-untyped-defs with the typed value flowing through (no signature change expected)."},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"Promote rebar.reducer.* into the tier-1 disallow_untyped_defs override list."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py","reason":"Pin rebar.reducer.* in _RATCHET_BASELINE (shrink-only ratchet)."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","eb49-3f52-e95e-4332"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"68101444-020f-45da-88df-bc78177c1f09","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d893-e003-0539-47fc","ticket_type":"task","title":"Give reducer._filters.match_predicate a typed predicate value so reducer can join the typing ratchet","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4f8c0e57-a77a-4147-ada2-b6c8040b7d5e","cc495a87-a413-4cf8-9623-3435f877bf37","030338e6-a323-4cf9-9e9d-56f57ddef488","182c038f-3654-4e49-b393-a6a7304603b9","5363039f-c3b9-4a57-9210-dd53d274d63d","f6ff83e6-c66d-453c-a78d-0cb955793064","c1e3706a-1720-459b-8607-6143e8fbc816","0f84bd43-6224-4cfe-b85c-c8a13836b00f","a0e5dc26-f1dd-486a-a5b0-29a86ac3b753","05bb5593-5142-4f49-8c71-a87487b1d9d8","6d8952dc-c71c-4341-aa8d-866e9ded6a61","68101444-020f-45da-88df-bc78177c1f09","671c3171-d36d-44e7-aadf-6fb676bc4613"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787400309142188104,"uuid":"69a9ac44-59a3-4048-b1f6-e492bc074024"}